#HSSS 1.0
TITLE: Ubuntu White Edition / glibc Specification
PACKAGE: glibc
LANGUAGE: C, architecture-specific low-level code
STATUS: W1
ROLE: Core C runtime, ABI, threading, memory, locale, dynamic linking

## PROGRAM
glibc supplies the central user-space C runtime and interfaces used by a large portion of the operating system.

## STRUCTURE
SOURCE: upstream GNU libc / Ubuntu package
BOUNDARY: application -> libc ABI -> kernel/system interfaces
WHITE_EDITION: conservative integration layer

## SPEC
- preserve ABI/API compatibility
- avoid unnecessary dynamic-linking changes
- document locale/runtime configuration
- require representative architecture testing
- preserve rollback capability

## QUALITY
TEST: upstream regressions, ABI review, dynamic linking, threading/process, locale, application startup, upgrade/rollback
ECONOMY: startup, memory, linking overhead, installed footprint

## SOURCE POLICY
Native changes require a demonstrated requirement. Architecture-specific changes require representative target testing. No speculative rewrites.
